    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n367" root="اخذ" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَأْخَذْ</span></b>  [<i>A place where,</i> or <i>whence, a thing is
taken:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَآخِذُ</span>.] [Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَآخِذُ الطَّيْرِ</span> <i>The
places whence birds are taken.</i> (K, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [<i>The
source of derivation</i> of a word or phrase or meaning.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>A way [which one takes];</i> as in the
phrase, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَأْخَذَ الأَقْرَبَ سَلَكَ</span> <i>He went the nearest
way.</i> (Msb. in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خصر</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  [See also 2, last
sentence but one.]

